# 30. Explain the difference between INNER JOIN, LEFT JOIN, RIGHT JOIN, and FULL OUTER JOIN.

This is one of the most important JOIN questions.

### INNER JOIN

Returns:

> Only matching records from both tables.

```text
A ∩ B
```

---

### LEFT JOIN

Returns:

> All records from the left table + matching records from the right.

```text
A + matching B
```

---

### RIGHT JOIN

Returns:

> All records from the right table + matching records from the left.

```text
B + matching A
```

---

### FULL OUTER JOIN

Returns:

> All records from both tables, whether they match or not.

```text
A + B
```

---

## Visual Summary

```text
          INNER JOIN
       Matching only

       ┌───────┐
       │   A   │
       │   ┌───┼───┐
       │   │███│   │
       └───┼───┘   │
           │   B   │
           └───────┘
```

Simpler to memorize:

| JOIN              | Result                    |
| ----------------- | ------------------------- |
| `INNER JOIN`      | Matching rows only        |
| `LEFT JOIN`       | All left + matching right |
| `RIGHT JOIN`      | All right + matching left |
| `FULL OUTER JOIN` | All rows from both        |

### 🎤 Interview Answer

> INNER JOIN returns only matching records from both tables. LEFT JOIN returns all records from the left table and matching records from the right. RIGHT JOIN does the opposite. FULL OUTER JOIN returns all records from both tables, including non-matching records.

